@startuml
title Campaign State Transition Diagram

[*] --> Idle

state "Idle" as Idle
state "Campaign Preparation" as CP
state "Advert Approval and Scheduling" as AAS
state "Running Adverts" as RA
state "Campaign Completion" as CC
state "Payment Processing" as PP
state "Refund Generation" as RG
state "Balance Settlement" as BS
state "Paid Campaign" as PC
state "Archived Campaign" as AC

Idle --> CP : Manager and Staff Assigned / Start Campaign
CP --> AAS : Everything Approved and Contract Signed / Activate Campaign
AAS --> RA : Adverts Prepared and Scheduled / Run Adverts
RA --> CC : All Adverts Finished / Complete Campaign
CC --> PP : Payment Processing Required / Handle Payment
PP --> RG : Amount Paid Less Than Required / Generate Refund
RG --> BS : Amount Paid Exceeds Required Amount / Wait for Balance Settlement
BS --> PC : Full Amount Properly Paid / Mark Campaign as Paid
PC --> AC : Campaign Completed and Staff Released / Archive Campaign

@enduml
